<title>JAPAN: Showa Denko alloy plant start-up nears.</title>
<headline>Showa Denko alloy plant start-up nears.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showa Denko plans to start regular production this month at its 40,000-tonne-per-year number three aluminium alloy plant in Chiba, near Tokyo, bringing total alloy capacity to 120,000 tonnes a year, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The refurbished number one plant, with a capacity of 80,000 tonnes per year, started commercial production in April. The company's aging number two plant was shut down last year, he added.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
